  + /// Grade a forecast that may be absent: an EMPTY prediction list yields
  + /// `None` (ungraded), never `Some(0.0)`. An empty list is the absence of a
  + /// forecast — "quiet because silent" — and must stay distinguishable from a
  + /// populated forecast that scored 0% ("quiet because right" on a green day,
  + /// a miss on a failure day). Day 143: this invariant used to live only as a
  + /// hand-copied guard at each call site (enforcement on the cooperative
  + /// path); it now lives in the shared layer so a future call site can't
  + /// forget it. Returns `Some((hits, accuracy_pct))` for populated forecasts.
